1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,127
JESUS: A new command I give you.

2
00:00:06,427 --> 00:00:07,999
JESUS: Love each other...

3
00:00:08,049 --> 00:00:09,946
JESUS: as I have loved you.

4
00:00:10,996 --> 00:00:14,325
He said this on the night He was betrayed...

5
00:00:14,425 --> 00:00:19,277
only moments after handing bread to the man who would betray Him.

6
00:00:24,027 --> 00:00:29,194
Behind this door, an old man waits to die... for the name of Jesus.

7
00:00:29,544 --> 00:00:34,309
And the man standing outside it... has hated him for most of his life.

8
00:00:36,658 --> 00:00:37,537
ASHER: Bread.

9
00:00:38,287 --> 00:00:40,837
ASHER: I came all this way... with bread.

10
00:00:41,487 --> 00:00:46,078
Months earlier, his church had gathered to hear a letter read aloud.

11
00:00:46,328 --> 00:00:51,054
ELDER: Paul, a servant of Christ Jesus... to all in Rome who are loved by God.

12
00:00:52,104 --> 00:00:54,954
ELDER: Do not repay anyone evil for evil.

13
00:00:55,204 --> 00:00:59,988
ELDER: If it is possible, as far as it depends on you... live at peace with everyone.

14
00:01:00,238 --> 00:01:05,138
ELDER: If your enemy is hungry, feed him. If he is thirsty, give him something to drink.

15
00:01:05,288 --> 00:01:08,810
ELDER: In doing this, you will heap burning coals on his head.

16
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:12,660
ASHER: His own words.

17
00:01:13,310 --> 00:01:14,996
ASHER: Let's see if he believes them.

18
00:01:17,946 --> 00:01:19,841
GUARD: Food for the old man?

19
00:01:20,091 --> 00:01:23,246
GUARD: You're the first one in a week. Make it quick.

20
00:01:25,796 --> 00:01:28,028
PAUL: Luke? ...Is that you?

21
00:01:29,078 --> 00:01:33,228
PAUL: No... forgive me. My eyes are not what they were.

22
00:01:33,378 --> 00:01:35,513
PAUL: Come in, friend. Come in.

23
00:01:35,763 --> 00:01:38,156
PAUL: Is that bread? God bless you.

24
00:01:38,406 --> 00:01:42,732
PAUL: Most of the brothers are afraid to come now. I don't blame them.

25
00:01:43,682 --> 00:01:45,596
ASHER: I'm not here because I'm brave.

26
00:01:46,246 --> 00:01:47,730
ASHER: You don't remember me.

27
00:01:48,580 --> 00:01:49,658
PAUL: Should I?

28
00:01:50,308 --> 00:01:52,826
ASHER: Jerusalem. The street of the potters.

29
00:01:53,076 --> 00:01:54,726
ASHER: A house with a blue door.

30
00:01:55,076 --> 00:01:58,022
ASHER: You came at night... with the temple guard.

31
00:01:58,672 --> 00:02:01,383
ASHER: You dragged a man named Yosef into the street.

32
00:02:01,533 --> 00:02:02,949
ASHER: In front of his wife.

33
00:02:02,999 --> 00:02:04,414
ASHER: In front of his son.

34
00:02:05,164 --> 00:02:06,689
PAUL: Yosef...

35
00:02:07,538 --> 00:02:12,070
ASHER: I was eight years old. I watched it all... through a crack in the door.

36
00:02:12,720 --> 00:02:14,372
ASHER: He never came home.

37
00:02:17,322 --> 00:02:18,931
PAUL: He looked at me.

38
00:02:19,481 --> 00:02:22,829
PAUL: When we bound his hands... he looked straight at me.

39
00:02:23,079 --> 00:02:26,019
PAUL: Not with hatred. I knew hatred.

40
00:02:26,369 --> 00:02:30,560
PAUL: He looked at me as if... as if he was sorry for me.

41
00:02:34,010 --> 00:02:35,220
YOUNG ASHER: Abba...

42
00:02:36,770 --> 00:02:39,536
YOSEF: Asher. Don't be afraid.

43
00:02:39,886 --> 00:02:42,662
YOSEF: Remember what He taught us.

44
00:02:42,912 --> 00:02:46,312
YOSEF: Love each other... as He loved us.

45
00:02:46,662 --> 00:02:47,552
SAUL: Take him!

46
00:02:53,702 --> 00:02:54,561
ASHER: Don't.

47
00:02:54,811 --> 00:02:57,788
ASHER: You don't get to remember him. He wasn't yours.

48
00:02:58,238 --> 00:02:59,477
PAUL: You're right.

49
00:02:59,827 --> 00:03:03,337
PAUL: He wasn't mine. I have no right to any of it.

50
00:03:04,987 --> 00:03:06,939
ASHER: They read your letter in our church.

51
00:03:07,189 --> 00:03:09,845
ASHER: “If your enemy is hungry, feed him.”

52
00:03:10,195 --> 00:03:11,732
ASHER: So. I'm feeding you.

53
00:03:13,882 --> 00:03:17,012
PAUL: Then you have done what I only wrote about.

54
00:03:17,362 --> 00:03:19,228
ASHER: Don't. Don't make me a saint.

55
00:03:19,478 --> 00:03:22,711
ASHER: They call you a saint. Do they even know what you were?

56
00:03:23,161 --> 00:03:24,264
PAUL: They know.

57
00:03:24,414 --> 00:03:28,202
PAUL: I put it in my letters, so that no one forgets.

58
00:03:28,552 --> 00:03:33,900
PAUL: I was a blasphemer... and a persecutor... and a violent man.

59
00:03:34,450 --> 00:03:37,052
PAUL: I thought I was defending God.

60
00:03:37,402 --> 00:03:39,173
PAUL: I was hunting Him.

61
00:03:39,923 --> 00:03:43,850
PAUL: I carried your father's face all the way to Damascus.

62
00:03:44,100 --> 00:03:46,895
PAUL: I had letters to arrest more of them.

63
00:03:50,845 --> 00:03:53,997
JESUS: Saul... Saul. Why do you persecute me?

64
00:03:54,447 --> 00:03:56,064
SAUL: Who are you, Lord?

65
00:03:56,614 --> 00:04:00,267
JESUS: I am Jesus... whom you are persecuting.

66
00:04:01,917 --> 00:04:03,909
PAUL: I knew what I deserved.

67
00:04:04,259 --> 00:04:07,975
PAUL: But He looked at me... the same way your father did.

68
00:04:08,425 --> 00:04:13,409
PAUL: I was shown mercy, because I acted in ignorance and unbelief.

69
00:04:13,559 --> 00:04:17,544
PAUL: The grace of our Lord was poured out on me abundantly...

70
00:04:17,564 --> 00:04:21,945
PAUL: along with the faith and love that are in Christ Jesus.

71
00:04:22,295 --> 00:04:26,585
PAUL: I thank Christ Jesus our Lord, who has given me strength...

72
00:04:26,635 --> 00:04:31,154
PAUL: that He considered me trustworthy, appointing me to His service.

73
00:04:31,504 --> 00:04:32,562
PAUL: Me.

74
00:04:33,312 --> 00:04:34,487
ASHER: So that's it?

75
00:04:34,737 --> 00:04:37,412
ASHER: You saw a light... and it all washed away?

76
00:04:37,762 --> 00:04:41,287
ASHER: And my father was just... the price of your conversion?

77
00:04:41,937 --> 00:04:42,953
PAUL: No.

78
00:04:43,303 --> 00:04:46,633
PAUL: Nothing washes him away. Not for me.

79
00:04:46,983 --> 00:04:51,556
PAUL: I see his face every time I write the word “mercy.”

80
00:04:52,806 --> 00:04:57,415
PAUL: Here is a trustworthy saying that deserves full acceptance:

81
00:04:57,565 --> 00:05:01,453
PAUL: Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners...

82
00:05:01,703 --> 00:05:04,180
PAUL: of whom I am the worst.

83
00:05:04,830 --> 00:05:08,170
PAUL: But for that very reason, I was shown mercy...

84
00:05:08,220 --> 00:05:14,470
PAUL: so that in me, the worst of sinners, Christ Jesus might display His immense patience...

85
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:20,106
PAUL: as an example for those who would believe in Him... and receive eternal life.

86
00:05:20,856 --> 00:05:22,496
ASHER: I came here to hate you.

87
00:05:23,046 --> 00:05:25,072
ASHER: I rehearsed it. For years.

88
00:05:25,421 --> 00:05:28,545
PAUL: I know. And I deserve every word.

89
00:05:28,895 --> 00:05:31,532
ASHER: That's the worst part. You do deserve it.

90
00:05:31,982 --> 00:05:33,197
ASHER: And I still...

91
00:05:33,547 --> 00:05:35,183
ASHER: I still brought the bread.

92
00:05:35,933 --> 00:05:37,941
YOSEF: Love each other...

93
00:05:37,961 --> 00:05:39,858
JESUS: as I have loved you.

94
00:05:47,008 --> 00:05:49,282
ASHER: My father would have broken it with you.

95
00:05:49,832 --> 00:05:51,877
ASHER: So... I will.

96
00:05:54,927 --> 00:05:56,736
PAUL: Burning coals...

97
00:05:57,286 --> 00:06:01,772
PAUL: I wrote those words. I never knew how much they burn.

98
00:06:02,522 --> 00:06:05,226
Do not be overcome by evil...

99
00:06:05,476 --> 00:06:08,149
but overcome evil with good.

100
00:06:10,099 --> 00:06:11,356
GUARD: Time's up.

101
00:06:11,706 --> 00:06:15,945
GUARD: And you, old man... it's tomorrow. First light. The road to Ostia.

102
00:06:16,894 --> 00:06:17,974
ASHER: Tomorrow?

103
00:06:18,423 --> 00:06:20,151
PAUL: Thank you, soldier.

104
00:06:20,401 --> 00:06:22,046
GUARD: Say your goodbyes.

105
00:06:22,996 --> 00:06:24,299
ASHER: Aren't you afraid?

106
00:06:25,249 --> 00:06:26,482
PAUL: Afraid?

107
00:06:26,832 --> 00:06:30,126
PAUL: Who shall separate us from the love of Christ?

108
00:06:30,376 --> 00:06:33,876
PAUL: Shall trouble, or hardship, or persecution...

109
00:06:33,896 --> 00:06:37,730
PAUL: or famine, or nakedness, or danger, or sword?

110
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:42,356
PAUL: As it is written: “For your sake we face death all day long;

111
00:06:42,375 --> 00:06:45,641
PAUL: we are considered as sheep to be slaughtered.”

112
00:06:45,991 --> 00:06:49,737
PAUL: No! In all these things we are more than conquerors...

113
00:06:49,757 --> 00:06:52,137
PAUL: through Him who loved us.

114
00:06:52,487 --> 00:06:55,926
PAUL: For I am convinced that neither death nor life,

115
00:06:55,946 --> 00:07:01,696
PAUL: neither angels nor demons, neither the present nor the future, nor any powers,

116
00:07:01,716 --> 00:07:06,164
PAUL: neither height nor depth, nor anything else in all creation...

117
00:07:06,214 --> 00:07:12,992
PAUL & ASHER: will be able to separate us from the love of God that is in Christ Jesus our Lord.

118
00:07:15,742 --> 00:07:20,823
At first light, the old man was led out along the road to Ostia.

119
00:07:21,173 --> 00:07:25,237
Among the few who followed him... was the son of Yosef.

120
00:07:27,187 --> 00:07:28,666
ASHER: Love each other...

121
00:07:28,816 --> 00:07:30,242
ASHER: as He loved us.

122
00:07:32,392 --> 00:07:34,289
JESUS: As I have loved you.

